<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adolf Hitler</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1889">1889</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adolf Hitler was the leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazi-party">Nazi Party</a> and dictator of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> from 1933 to 1945. Appointed chancellor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar-republic">Weimar Republic</a> in January 1933, he quickly abolished democracy and built a totalitarian state. His expansionist wars began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> in 1939, and his regime carried out the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a>. He killed himself in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> in April 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler.jpg" alt="Adolf Hitler" width="320" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heinrich Hoffmann · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hitler_portrait_crop_(cropped)(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
